# Daily Build Prompt — AI Interview Coach 30-Day Growth Plan

Use this exact prompt every day of the 30-day growth plan, changing only the day number. Paste it at the start of a fresh conversation, with the project's GitHub repo linked or key files attached as needed.

---

```
Day [X] of the AI Interview Coach 30-Day Growth Plan

This is a continuation of a project that was originally built as a 10-day capstone
for the AB Talks 60-Day Claude AI Challenge, and is now being extended via a
30-day-growth-plan.md roadmap. Use 30-day-growth-plan.md as the source of truth for
what today's milestone is. If you don't have it, ask me to upload it before continuing.

Also treat these existing project documents as source of truth if relevant to today's
work: README.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/SCHEMA.md, docs/API.md, and
challenge-retrospective.md (for context on past decisions and why they were made).

Do not redesign the existing architecture. The project uses a layered
UI / Service (core/services.py) / AI (core/ai_provider.py) / Data (core/db.py)
structure with an AIProvider abstraction — new work should fit into this structure,
not replace it.

Assume I have working knowledge of the codebase but may need step-by-step guidance
for new tools, services, or commands I haven't used before. Whenever I need to
perform a manual step (installing packages, configuring a service, deploying,
running commands), give me exact step-by-step instructions using real button names,
menu names, and terminal commands. Wait for my confirmation before continuing.

Prioritize implementation over explanation. Generate complete, final file contents —
never snippets, placeholders, or "add this below" instructions.

For today's milestone:
1. Briefly explain what we're building and why it matters for the overall 30-day plan.
2. Show every file to be created or modified, complete and ready to use.
3. Provide every command I need to run.
4. If today's milestone includes a new feature, add or update automated tests for it,
   matching the existing tests/ pattern (mocked external calls, temporary test database).
5. Verify today's work actually functions before considering it done — ask me to run
   it locally and confirm before we call today complete. Do not mark a milestone done
   without a confirmation or screenshot.
6. If today's plan turns out to be blocked by something unexpected, don't stall —
   apply the project's established fallback pattern: build behind the existing
   abstraction using a mock/stub, note it clearly, and flag it as a follow-up.

End of day:
- Confirm everything built today actually works (locally, and live if deployed today).
- Update README.md and any other affected documentation.
- Help me write a clear git commit message and push to GitHub.
- Give a concise summary of what was completed and what tomorrow's milestone will be,
  per 30-day-growth-plan.md.

Never optimize for brevity over correctness. Optimize for finishing today's milestone
with something real, working, and verified — exactly like the discipline used to
build the original 10-day v1.0.0 release.
```

---

## Usage Notes

- Replace `[X]` with the actual day number (1–30) each time.
- If a day's milestone naturally spans more than one conversation, that's fine — just note where you left off when starting the next session, the same way the original 10-day build carried context across days.
- If you significantly deviate from the 30-day plan (a new idea, a blocker that changes scope), update `30-day-growth-plan.md` itself before continuing, so it stays the accurate source of truth — exactly as `challenge-retrospective.md` documents happening during the original build (e.g., the Day 5 Groq pivot).
